WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:02.709
INTRO:
SnapChat is one of the most popular social

00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:07.819
media platforms in the world especially amongst
gen Z.

00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:12.480
Amongst many teengagers and young adults,
Snap has become a verb similar to Google or

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.480
Venmo.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.400
Yet, despite their popularity, like most tech
companies and startups, they’ve lost money

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.939
for most of their life.

00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:25.180
In fact, the last quarter of 2021 was the
first profitable quarter in the company’s

00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:27.340
history as a public company.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.359
SnapChat proudly announced this news near
the top of their quarterly report likely with

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:33.730
optimistic expectations for the stock.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:38.610
Yet, it’s been months since this report
came out, and SnapChat stock is still doing

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:40.880
worse than ever before.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:46.690
Since their peak in September of 2021, SnapChat
fell a total of 70% which correlates to a

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.820
market cap loss of $95.8 billion or nearly
$100 billion.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:57.070
Over the past several weeks, they have recovered
a substantial amount, rallying over 50%.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:03.590
But, even with this significant rally, they’re
still down over 50% from their all time high.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.880
So, what happened to SnapChat?

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:14.240
HISTORICALLY BAD:
Taking a look back, such terrible stock performance

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:16.910
is unfortunately not new to SnapChat.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:22.080
In fact, for most of SnapChat’s public life,
their stock price has performed horrendously.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:27.660
Right after SnapChat set an all time high
following their IPO, they proceeded to crash

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:29.340
83%.

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.500
And this wasn’t some quick 3 or 4 month
crash like the Covid crash either.

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:37.310
This was a long and drawn out sell off that
lasted nearly 2 years.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:43.030
By the time the sell off ended, SnapChat was
literally a penny stock coming in at less

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:44.910
than $5 a share.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:48.460
This wasn’t to say that SnapChat was fundamentally
performing bad though.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:54.000
In fact, SnapChat is yet to even have a single
negative quarter in terms of revenue growth.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.200
Nonetheless, it seems like investors don’t
want any part of SnapChat, and that brings

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.890
us into SnapChat’s first shortfall which
is a lack of a strong investor base.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:08.789
Despite being on the market for over 5 years
now, SnapChat has struggled to attract investors

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:11.120
because they lack a differentiating factor.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:16.370
Now, users of SnapChat would likely disagree
with this statement given that despite Facebook

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:20.500
and YouTube’s best attempts to replicate
the best features of SnapChat like stories,

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:25.340
most SnapChat users have preferred to continue
using SnapChat for specific use cases.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:29.920
It seems like SnapChat has mastered casual
conversations better than any of their competitors.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.790
But, from an investor's perspective, who cares
if SnapChat fulfills some niche role within

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:36.320
young adults lives?

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:39.880
On paper, Instagram is superior in almost
every way.

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:45.220
For example, in terms of demographics, 18-24
year olds are SnapChat’s biggest customer

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:49.890
base with 13-17 year olds making up nearly
a quarter of their user base.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:54.920
Meanwhile, Instagram’s largest demographic
is 25-34 year olds with second place going

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.090
to 18-24 year olds.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:02.310
Instagram’s 13-17 year old base is almost
non-existent while their 35 years and up demographic

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:03.950
is actually quite substantial.

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:08.910
Now, if newer generations don’t switch over
to using Instagram, that could be a long term

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:09.910
problem.

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:14.260
But, for the time being, Instagram has no
shortage of users, and all of their users

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.480
are significantly older than SnapChat users
which means that they have more money, are

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:21.730
more monetizable, and are of course more profitable.

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:26.470
This directly aligns with household incomes
studies conducted on both platforms as well.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:32.550
SnapChat use is most common amongst households
with incomes between $70 and $80,000 per year.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:37.740
Meanwhile, Instagram use is most common amongst
households with incomes above $100,000 per

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:38.740
year.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:41.860
Again users with more money equals more profits.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.459
Something else to note about SnapChat’s
demographics is that it's mostly just limited

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:46.959
to the US.

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:52.120
SnapChat has 109.5 million users within the
US which is nearly more than all of their

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.060
users in all these countries combined.

00:03:54.060 --> 00:03:58.690
If we take a look at Instagram’s usage by
country, we can clearly see that it's a lot

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:01.349
more spread out, especially amongst emerging
countries.

00:04:01.349 --> 00:04:05.800
So, from an investors perspective, there’s
very little reason to bet on SnapChat over

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:06.920
Facebook.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:10.890
If you want to target millennials and older,
Instagrams the way to go.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:15.020
If you want to target people with money, Instagrams
the way to go.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.079
If you want to target emerging countries,
Instagram is the way to go.

00:04:19.079 --> 00:04:22.759
The only reason to invest in SnapChat is if
you think that younger generations in the

00:04:22.759 --> 00:04:27.589
US will continue to use SnapChat over Instagram
which could very well be true.

00:04:27.589 --> 00:04:31.169
But for this to become a financial advantage
for SnapChat, we’ll likely have to wait

00:04:31.169 --> 00:04:33.599
another 5 to 10 years at the very least.

00:04:33.599 --> 00:04:38.969
And, in the meantime, SnapChat will likely
remain the underdog amongst investors.

00:04:38.969 --> 00:04:45.000
APPLE PRIVACY CHANGES:
Aside from SnapChat’s unlucrative demographic,

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.360
SnapChat was also hit hard with Apple’s
privacy changes that rolled out last year.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:53.379
If you guys aren’t aware of this yet, in
April of 2021, Apple rolled out a feature

00:04:53.379 --> 00:04:55.690
called App Tracking Transparency.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:59.330
This feature allows users to choose if they
want to let third party apps collect data

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:02.210
regarding their usage for advertising purposes.

00:05:02.210 --> 00:05:05.569
And as you would guess, basically everyone
opted out.

00:05:05.569 --> 00:05:11.249
According to this study, only 4% of Americans
were opting in to tracking, and I have a feeling

00:05:11.249 --> 00:05:14.870
that a lot of these guys may have accidentally
pressed allow.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.619
SnapChat’s CEO Evan Spiegel was actually
a big proponent of this move.

00:05:19.619 --> 00:05:24.229
In fact, he believes that these privacy changes
were good for iPhone consumers and the social

00:05:24.229 --> 00:05:26.569
media ecosystem in general.

00:05:26.569 --> 00:05:32.000
But, despite his moral support for the change,
this change was obviously not good for SnapChat’s

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.000
financials.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.500
In October of 2021, Evan announced that Apple’s
privacy changes have actually been affecting

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.849
revenue more than they originally anticipated.

00:05:39.849 --> 00:05:44.469
And to make things worse, SnapChat failed
to meet investors' already conservative revenue

00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:47.680
estimates which of course sent the stock tumbling.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.879
Given this unfavorable situation, Evan has
chosen to focus on profitability which he

00:05:51.879 --> 00:05:52.879
did accomplish.

00:05:52.879 --> 00:05:56.710
But, this has left many investors wondering,
at what cost?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:06:02.119
Sure, it’s nice to invest in a profitable
company, but the primary reason most SnapChat

00:06:02.119 --> 00:06:05.129
investors made the investment was because
of growth expectations.

00:06:05.129 --> 00:06:10.509
And now it seems like Evan is trying to appease
investors with relatively small profits.

00:06:10.509 --> 00:06:16.159
SnapChat doesn’t have a PE ratio quite yet
as that requires a full year of profitability,

00:06:16.159 --> 00:06:21.249
but even if we take their net income of $22.55
million from last quarter and extrapolate

00:06:21.249 --> 00:06:24.990
it to a year, we only get about $100 million.

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:29.999
Now, this isn’t a bad amount by any means,
but compared to their market cap, this gives

00:06:29.999 --> 00:06:33.610
them a PE ratio of 673.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:38.270
Even if we say that SnapChat’s profitability
grows to $250 million per quarter or over

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:44.699
10x from where they are currently, their PE
ratio would still be quite high at 67.3.

00:06:44.699 --> 00:06:48.770
To put that in perspective, Facebook’s PE
ratio is under 20.

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:52.539
This isn’t exactly a bad thing given that
SnapChat should theoretically have a lot more

00:06:52.539 --> 00:06:57.060
growth left than Facebook, but that’s the
key, they need to have growth.

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:01.500
And with Apple’s recent privacy policy changes
and potentially more on the way, investors

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:04.569
aren’t quite convinced to give SnapChat
even more credit.

00:07:04.569 --> 00:07:11.189
THE TIK TOK PHENOMENON:
At this point, you may be thinking what could

00:07:11.189 --> 00:07:15.649
possibly be worse than having slower growth
and a less profitable user base.

00:07:15.649 --> 00:07:19.020
Well, the answer is being replaced.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:24.370
But wait a minute, SnapChat has a massive
user base, most of whom are young, so SnapChat

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:27.189
won’t be going anywhere anytime soon right?

00:07:27.189 --> 00:07:32.909
Well, while that may be true, that doesn’t
prevent an old or new competitor from overtaking

00:07:32.909 --> 00:07:33.909
SnapChat.

00:07:33.909 --> 00:07:35.669
Just take a look at TikTok.

00:07:35.669 --> 00:07:40.059
TikTok wasn’t released till September of
2016, yet it was the most visited site in

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:41.400
the world in 2021.

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:47.129
This isn’t to say that it’s easy to replicate
TikTok’s success, but it makes it clear

00:07:47.129 --> 00:07:50.830
that the barrier for entry is extremely low
within the social media industry.

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:55.550
From an app development perspective, it’s
not particularly hard to create a social media

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:56.550
app.

00:07:56.550 --> 00:08:02.899
What’s hard is garnering users and 99.999%
of social media apps will never garner the

00:08:02.899 --> 00:08:05.589
same user base as someone like SnapChat or
Facebook.

00:08:05.589 --> 00:08:10.789
But, from SnapChat’s perspective, only 1
or 2 of the millions of social media apps

00:08:10.789 --> 00:08:15.629
out there need to catch on for SnapChat to
lose user engagement to these new apps.

00:08:15.629 --> 00:08:20.370
And from a user's perspective, if a new better
app comes out, the only thing stopping you

00:08:20.370 --> 00:08:23.689
from switching over is your social circle
also switching over.

00:08:23.689 --> 00:08:27.640
If your social circle also switches over,
you’ll probably never look back, and this

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:31.129
has been shown time and time again within
the social media industry.

00:08:31.129 --> 00:08:36.070
First, there was Friendster, then there was
MySpace, then we had Facebook and Twitter,

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:39.950
and after that we had Instagram and WhatsApp,
and now we have SnapChat.

00:08:39.950 --> 00:08:44.260
What’s to say that SnapChat wont eventually
be phased out as well?

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:48.970
Well, the truth is that all companies are
eventually phased out, it’s just that the

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:53.140
phase at the top is rather short lived for
social media companies due to the low barrier

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:54.380
of entry.

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:55.710
Take Apple for example.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:09:00.160
They also won’t stay at the top forever,
but think about how much more difficult it

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:04.060
is for a company to come out with a smartphone
and convince you to pay several hundred dollars

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:08.010
for it as opposed to an app developer coming
out with a new social media app and convincing

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:09.640
you to give it a shot.

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:15.350
Obviously, the latter is magnitudes easier
which is great for competition and evolution,

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.300
but not great for investors.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:19.910
For example, just take a look at Twitter stock.

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.160
They really haven’t moved in nearly a decade.

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:28.890
Not to mention, Twitter has become unprofitable
once again, and Jack Dorsey has left the company.

00:09:28.890 --> 00:09:33.410
Really, the only social media stock that has
performed extremely well historically is Facebook,

00:09:33.410 --> 00:09:37.210
and that’s mainly thanks to their acquisitions
of WhatsApp and Instagram.

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:42.000
Also, something to note about Facebook is
that while they have performed well financially,

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.460
they’re one of the most hated if not the
most hated company in the world.

00:09:46.460 --> 00:09:51.250
So, I don’t think that’s necessarily something
that SnapChat should strive for.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:55.271
But at the same time, if they don’t make
acquisitions and become the big tech company

00:09:55.271 --> 00:09:59.520
that everyone hates, it’s just a matter
of time until the new kid on the block overtakes

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:01.420
them anyway.

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:06.490
SNAPCHAT’S FUTURE:
While this video has mostly pointed out the

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:10.650
shortfalls of SnapChat and the social media
industry, I don’t think SnapChat is going

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.770
anywhere anytime soon.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:16.830
They just became profitable, their user base
is just starting to make money, and there’s

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:19.170
still plenty of user growth left for SnapChat.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:23.950
So, I don’t think SnapChat has really hit
their stride yet, meaning that SnapChat stock

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:26.470
likely has a lot of upside ahead.

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:30.780
But with that being said, I don’t think
SnapChat is a lifelong long hold like many

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:36.280
other investments such as the S&amp;P 500, Tesla,
Bitcoin, Ethereum, etc.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:41.710
Whether SnapChat peaks at a market cap of
$300 billion or a market cap of $1 trillion,

00:10:41.710 --> 00:10:45.830
I think it’s just a matter of time until
they’re phased out, and I think the next

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.500
wave of phasing will be extremely painful.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:53.020
I think the next phase will not only be a
move away from SnapChat, but a move away from

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.530
traditional social media apps in general.

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:59.310
With more people being aware of how these
companies make money, an increasing concern

00:10:59.310 --> 00:11:04.080
for privacy, and more backlash than ever before
against big tech, I think it’s highly likely

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:08.150
that the next big social media app will be
some sort of decentralized or non profit endeavor

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:09.150
like Signal.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:13.400
I suspect Mark Zuckerberg has similar beliefs,
and that’s why he cut back on social media

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:16.460
acquisitions and is betting it all on the
Metaverse.

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:20.420
With that being said, I think an investment
into SnapChat would be more of a median horizon

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:23.020
investment of 10 to 15 years.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:26.350
You may be able to get in, make a solid 10X
and get out.

00:11:26.350 --> 00:11:31.420
But, in my opinion, if you’re gonna commit
to a stock for 10 to 15 years, why not commit

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:36.300
to something you can hold for life that can
produce 30, 40, or 50X return?

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.660
But, that’s just what I think.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:40.230
Would you guys invest in SnapChat?

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:41.540
